  "symbols": {
    "why": "Overlined numbers are depths in feet, circled ones ceiling-to-floor heights in feet, 'p.' penetrations in feet. On this photo OCR found 7 of the 25 depths, 4 of the 7 penetrations and none of the 12 circled heights; as their labels are excluded from the trace (their dark text read as fill), all are listed here by hand, each checked on a crop (the circled 19 in the glare and the circled 1 at the south-west end are blurred). One water-movement sign (wavy line with its head, pointing about south) in the passage west of 37. The only letter like the legend's B is a small blurred bold mark at a side passage's mouth (B or R: kept as bones, to check); an R by p.1062. 'The Tres Estrelas connection' is the leads-to at p.2308. The straight arrow by the circled 19 is taken for a cross-section mark (its section is just north), not water movement.",
